window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-050.json",{"day":50,"title":"When Workers Bought Their Own Factory","targetWords":[{"word":"grind","gloss":"磨","context":"The small clothing factory had survived on machines that could grind metal parts, hoist heavy rolls, and keep production moving through long shifts.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"hoist","gloss":"吊起","context":"The small clothing factory had survived on machines that could grind metal parts, hoist heavy rolls, and keep production moving through long shifts.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"humiliate","gloss":"羞辱","context":"Its owner would sometimes humiliate a worker for a mistake or hurl an unfinished garment onto the floor.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"hurl","gloss":"猛扔","context":"Its owner would sometimes humiliate a worker for a mistake or hurl an unfinished garment onto the floor.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"overthrow","gloss":"推翻","context":"Employees did not initially want to overthrow management; they wanted reliable wages and safe conditions.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"scramble","gloss":"仓促行动","context":"When closure was announced, they had to scramble for alternatives.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"stun","gloss":"使震惊","context":"The news could stun even experienced staff.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"bait","gloss":"诱饵","context":"An outside buyer offered attractive promises as bait, but workers first inspected each bearing and electrical coil to learn whether the business could be run on less exploitative terms.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"bearing","gloss":"轴承","context":"An outside buyer offered attractive promises as bait, but workers first inspected each bearing and electrical coil to learn whether the business could be run on less exploitative terms.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"clap","gloss":"鼓掌","context":"At a meeting, people did not immediately clap for the idea of collective ownership.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"clutch","gloss":"紧握","context":"One seamstress continued to clutch her wage slip while asking difficult questions.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"coil","gloss":"线圈","context":"An outside buyer offered attractive promises as bait, but workers first inspected each bearing and electrical coil to learn whether the business could be run on less exploitative terms.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"denounce","gloss":"谴责","context":"They could denounce injustice without letting uncertain prospects depress them into silence.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"depress","gloss":"使沮丧","context":"They could denounce injustice without letting uncertain prospects depress them into silence.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"fabricate","gloss":"编造","context":"Nobody should fabricate an account of guaranteed success.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"lick","gloss":"舔","context":"A clerk would lick an envelope to send a proposal, but paperwork must not obstruct genuine discussion.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"obstruct","gloss":"阻碍","context":"A clerk would lick an envelope to send a proposal, but paperwork must not obstruct genuine discussion.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"retort","gloss":"反驳","context":"A sharp retort was less useful than a clear explanation.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"sew","gloss":"缝","context":"Workers who could sew skillfully or zip a jacket perfectly did not automatically understand business loans.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"zip","gloss":"拉上拉链","context":"Workers who could sew skillfully or zip a jacket perfectly did not automatically understand business loans.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"agitate","gloss":"鼓动","context":"Organizers sought to agitate for change while admitting the new skills their colleagues would need.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"deduct","gloss":"扣除","context":"A new agreement would deduct a modest contribution only with each member's approval.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"drip","gloss":"滴落","context":"Maintenance came first: oil should not drip onto cloth, and newcomers could enquire about any unfamiliar machine.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"enquire","gloss":"询问","context":"Maintenance came first: oil should not drip onto cloth, and newcomers could enquire about any unfamiliar machine.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"giggle","gloss":"咯咯笑","context":"Young apprentices might giggle during a break, while veterans would mutter about past promises.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"mutter","gloss":"嘟囔","context":"Young apprentices might giggle during a break, while veterans would mutter about past promises.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"overhear","gloss":"偶然听到","context":"Rather than merely overhear those doubts, the organizers asked people to discuss them openly.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"reel","gloss":"摇晃","context":"Costs might make a hopeful buyer reel, and a poor estimate could stagger the entire group.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"relish","gloss":"享受","context":"Still, workers could relish the prospect of sharing decisions.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"stagger","gloss":"使吃惊","context":"Costs might make a hopeful buyer reel, and a poor estimate could stagger the entire group.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"streamline","gloss":"简化","context":"They began to streamline orders, inspect equipment that would vibrate excessively, and prevent loose fabric from catching in parts that whirl at speed.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"vibrate","gloss":"振动","context":"They began to streamline orders, inspect equipment that would vibrate excessively, and prevent loose fabric from catching in parts that whirl at speed.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"whirl","gloss":"旋转","context":"They began to streamline orders, inspect equipment that would vibrate excessively, and prevent loose fabric from catching in parts that whirl at speed.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"wrench","gloss":"扳手","context":"A mechanic used a wrench to brace a damaged frame, while tailors checked whether a wrinkle was caused by fabric or handling.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"wrinkle","gloss":"皱褶","context":"A mechanic used a wrench to brace a damaged frame, while tailors checked whether a wrinkle was caused by fabric or handling.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"brace","gloss":"支撑","context":"A mechanic used a wrench to brace a damaged frame, while tailors checked whether a wrinkle was caused by fabric or handling.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"despatch","gloss":"发送","context":"Before they could despatch the first order, members had to distill their discussions into written rules.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"distill","gloss":"提炼","context":"Before they could despatch the first order, members had to distill their discussions into written rules.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"lash","gloss":"猛烈冲击","context":"A sudden drop in sales might lash their finances, so they began with a limited batch of pants.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"pants","gloss":"裤子","context":"A sudden drop in sales might lash their finances, so they began with a limited batch of pants.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"peep","gloss":"偷看","context":"Inspectors could peep through a machine's protective window, but never remove the guard to obtain a better view.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"quiver","gloss":"颤抖","context":"A nervous hand might quiver, and staff should not dismiss someone who paused to sniff a suspicious smell.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"sniff","gloss":"嗅","context":"A nervous hand might quiver, and staff should not dismiss someone who paused to sniff a suspicious smell.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"sprinkle","gloss":"撒","context":"Cleaners would sprinkle approved powder only where instructions permitted it, not improvise around electrical equipment.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"wink","gloss":"眨眼","context":"No reassuring wink from a manager could replace a sound financial plan.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"company","gloss":"公司","context":"The new company had to remain a viable business, with a realistic number of customers and enough money to survive delayed payments.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"business","gloss":"企业","context":"An outside buyer offered attractive promises as bait, but workers first inspected each bearing and electrical coil to learn whether the business could be run on less exploitative terms.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"number","gloss":"数量","context":"The new company had to remain a viable business, with a realistic number of customers and enough money to survive delayed payments.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"money","gloss":"钱","context":"The new company had to remain a viable business, with a realistic number of customers and enough money to survive delayed payments.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"bank","gloss":"银行","context":"A bank offered a small loan after reviewing the members' commitments and their revised costs.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"The small clothing factory had survived on machines that could grind metal parts, hoist heavy rolls, and keep production moving through long shifts. Its owner would sometimes humiliate a worker for a mistake or hurl an unfinished garment onto the floor. Employees did not initially want to overthrow management; they wanted reliable wages and safe conditions. When closure was announced, they had to scramble for alternatives. The news could stun even experienced staff. An outside buyer offered attractive promises as bait, but workers first inspected each bearing and electrical coil to learn whether the business could be run on less exploitative terms.","zh":"这家小服装厂依靠能磨金属部件、吊起沉重布卷，并在长班次中维持生产的机器生存。老板有时因失误羞辱工人，或把未完成衣服猛扔到地上。员工最初并不想推翻管理层，只希望工资可靠、条件安全。关厂消息公布后，他们必须仓促寻找替代方案。消息连老员工都可能震惊。一位外部买家拿诱人承诺作诱饵，但工人先检查每个轴承与电线圈，了解企业是否能以较少剥削的方式经营。"},{"en":"At a meeting, people did not immediately clap for the idea of collective ownership. One seamstress continued to clutch her wage slip while asking difficult questions. They could denounce injustice without letting uncertain prospects depress them into silence. Nobody should fabricate an account of guaranteed success. A clerk would lick an envelope to send a proposal, but paperwork must not obstruct genuine discussion. A sharp retort was less useful than a clear explanation. Workers who could sew skillfully or zip a jacket perfectly did not automatically understand business loans. Organizers sought to agitate for change while admitting the new skills their colleagues would need.","zh":"会上，大家没有立即为集体所有制鼓掌。一位女裁缝始终握着工资单，提出困难问题。他们可以谴责不公，却不让不确定前景把自己压得沉默。谁也不应编造成功有保证的说法。文员会舔湿信封寄送提案，但手续不能阻碍真正讨论。尖刻反驳不如清楚解释有用。能熟练缝纫或完美拉好外套拉链的工人，并不自动懂企业贷款。组织者鼓动变革，同时承认同事需要学习新技能。"},{"en":"A new agreement would deduct a modest contribution only with each member's approval. Maintenance came first: oil should not drip onto cloth, and newcomers could enquire about any unfamiliar machine. Young apprentices might giggle during a break, while veterans would mutter about past promises. Rather than merely overhear those doubts, the organizers asked people to discuss them openly. Costs might make a hopeful buyer reel, and a poor estimate could stagger the entire group. Still, workers could relish the prospect of sharing decisions. They began to streamline orders, inspect equipment that would vibrate excessively, and prevent loose fabric from catching in parts that whirl at speed.","zh":"新协议只在每位成员同意后扣除少量出资。维护优先：油不应滴到布上，新人可以询问任何不熟悉的机器。年轻学徒休息时可能咯咯笑，老员工则会嘟囔过去的承诺。组织者不只是偶然听见这些疑虑，而是请大家公开讨论。成本可能让满怀希望的购买者动摇，糟糕估计也可能震动整个团体。但工人仍能享受共同决策的前景。他们开始简化订单，检查振动过大的设备，并避免松散布料卷进高速旋转的部件。"},{"en":"A mechanic used a wrench to brace a damaged frame, while tailors checked whether a wrinkle was caused by fabric or handling. Before they could despatch the first order, members had to distill their discussions into written rules. A sudden drop in sales might lash their finances, so they began with a limited batch of pants. Inspectors could peep through a machine's protective window, but never remove the guard to obtain a better view. A nervous hand might quiver, and staff should not dismiss someone who paused to sniff a suspicious smell. Cleaners would sprinkle approved powder only where instructions permitted it, not improvise around electrical equipment.","zh":"机械工用扳手加固受损机架，裁缝检查皱褶是布料还是操作造成的。发出首批订单前，成员必须把讨论提炼成书面规则。销售突然下降可能猛烈冲击财务，因此他们先做有限数量的裤子。检查者可以透过机器防护窗查看，却不能为看得更清楚而移走护罩。紧张的手可能颤抖，员工也不应嘲笑停下来嗅可疑气味的人。清洁人员只在指示允许之处撒认可的粉剂，不能在电气设备附近随意试验。"},{"en":"No reassuring wink from a manager could replace a sound financial plan. The new company had to remain a viable business, with a realistic number of customers and enough money to survive delayed payments. A bank offered a small loan after reviewing the members' commitments and their revised costs. The purchase did not end disagreement, nor did it remove market risk. It changed who could inspect the accounts and influence decisions. For the workers, ownership meant accepting that responsibility together. Their achievement was neither effortless freedom nor instant prosperity, but the chance to connect skilled labor with a fairer voice in the enterprise it sustained.","zh":"管理者安抚性的眨眼不能代替稳健财务计划。新公司必须保持企业可行性，拥有现实数量的客户和足够资金，以应对延迟付款。银行审查成员承诺与调整后的成本后，提供小额贷款。收购并未结束分歧，也未消除市场风险，而是改变了谁能查看账目、影响决策。对工人来说，所有权意味着共同承担责任。他们的成就既不是不费力的自由，也不是立即富裕，而是有机会把熟练劳动与对其支撑的企业更公平的发言权联系起来。"}],"previous":49,"next":51});
